@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 1) Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newadmin",
  "password": "AdminPassword123!",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 2) Login and get JWT token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newadmin",
  "password": "AdminPassword123!"
}

### 3) Create an audit event (AUDIT_WRITER or ADMIN only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventType": "USER_LOGIN",
  "actorId": "newadmin",
  "resourceType": "APPLICATION",
  "resourceId": "APP-001",
  "payload": {
    "action": "logged_in",
    "ipAddress": "10.0.0.12",
    "status": "success"
  }
}

### 4) List audit events with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Get audit event by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6) Search events by resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/search/by-resource?resourceType=APPLICATION&resourceId=APP-001&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7) Search events by actor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/search/by-actor?actorId=newadmin&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8) Search events by type
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/search/by-type?eventType=USER_LOGIN&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9) Search events by time range
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/search/by-time-range?startTime=2026-01-01T00:00:00&endTime=2026-12-31T23:59:59&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10) Verify complete hash chain
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/verify-chain
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11) Verify a single event integrity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/1/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12) Archive an audit event (ADMIN only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/1/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13) Get audit event stats summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/events/stats/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14) Generate compliance report
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/reports/compliance?startDate=2026-01-01T00:00:00&endDate=2026-12-31T23:59:59
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15) Generate user audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/reports/user-audit-trail?actorId=newadmin&days=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16) Generate resource audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/reports/resource-audit-trail?resourceType=APPLICATION&resourceId=APP-001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17) Perform compliance check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18) Apply retention policy
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/retention/apply?retentionDays=365
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19) Redact event fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/redact/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fields": ["payload.ipAddress", "resourceId"],
  "reason": "PII redaction",
  "redactedBy": "newadmin"
}

### 20) Export audit events as JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/export/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 21) Export audit events as CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/export/csv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22) Generate audit report
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/compliance/reports/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23) Example role-specific login (AUDITOR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "auditorUser",
  "password": "AuditorPassword123!"
}

### 24) Example role-specific login (AUDIT_WRITER)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "writerUser",
  "password": "WriterPassword123!"
}
